# A template of a script: run as `script` is, with `@NOPROBE@` replaced by
# the path of a program that exits 3 whatever it is given. `:restart` into
# it is refused when its probe fails: the echo says so, no record is
# written, and the script goes on in this process with the session as it
# was. What it prints must be exactly `probe-expected`.

reload
settle
resize 640 480
key : Semicolon shift
commit e @FILE@
key <Enter> Enter -
indexed
key i KeyI -
key x KeyX -
key <Escape> Escape -
indexed
journalled
key : Semicolon shift
commit restart @NOPROBE@
key <Enter> Enter -
join
scene
